<%#
  The generic "coming soon" fallback for a calculator that is registry-active (its
  Calculators::X class is on `main`, so the slug resolves and the catalog knows it) but
  whose bespoke page has not shipped yet — the backend-before-frontend merge window
  (issue #214). Without this, CalculatorsController#show's `render "calculators/<slug>"`
  raised ActionView::MissingTemplate → a user-facing 500. This page degrades that into an
  intentional, on-brand "we're building it" state.

  STABLE PATH — the backend follow-up (the controller `rescue_from ActionView::MissingTemplate`
  for the direct-URL case) renders exactly this template: `render "calculators/unavailable"`.
  Do NOT rename without updating that controller hand-off.

  The controller sets `@calculator` to the looked-up Calculators::X class (it responds to
  `.slug`); `calculator_display_name` resolves a human name from the registry, falling back
  to a titleized slug — so this renders even before the INVENTORY row is ingested. It is
  defensive about `@calculator` being nil (a future caller may render it without one).

  BLEND (DESIGN.md): a surface card with the 5px coral left rule (the Hero-result frame,
  §4) reframed as a status, a green eyebrow (§2), warm copy, and a coral secondary button
  back to the catalog. No result UI, no form — there is nothing to compute yet.
%>

<% name = @calculator ? calculator_display_name(@calculator) : "This calculator" %>
<% content_for :title, "#{name} — coming soon — whizwheel" %>

<section class="mx-auto max-w-2xl">
  <%# Hero-result card frame (DESIGN.md §4): surface card, 5px coral left rule. %>
  <div class="rounded-[18px] border border-border border-l-[5px] border-l-primary bg-surface p-8 shadow-[0_10px_34px_rgba(150,110,80,0.12)] sm:p-10">
    <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-accent">Coming soon</p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-[-0.035em] text-ink">
      <%= name %>
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-xl text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
      This calculator is being built. The math is ready behind the scenes — we're putting
      the finishing touches on its page, and it will be available here shortly. Every answer
      is computed server-side and verifiable to the decimal.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
      <%= link_to "Browse all calculators", root_path,
            class: "inline-block rounded-[13px] bg-primary px-5 py-2.5 text-sm font-semibold text-surface shadow-sm transition-opacity hover:opacity-90 focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-accent" %>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
